        "image": "/bluebook-assets/Chapter05-ExcelSupercharged-EN.png",
        "markdown": "\nBelow Library is Multidimensional Tables — the structured\\-data workspace built into Basil\\.\n\nIf you're an Excel power user — VLOOKUPs, pivot tables, complex models — keep using Excel for what it does best\\. Multidimensional Tables aren't a replacement for it\\. They're where structured data lives inside Basil, so the Agent can query and update it directly\\. Here's what they add:\n\n|Capability|Excel|Basil Multidimensional Tables|\n|---|---|---|\n|Store structured data|✅|✅|\n|Store documents and images in a cell|Limited|✅|\n|Extract structured data from unstructured content|❌|✅|\n|Filters, views, conditional queries|✅ \\(filters, pivot tables\\)|✅ — plus saved views shareable as links|\n|Connected to your AI Agent|❌|✅ — the Agent queries tables directly and returns results|\n\nThe real magic happens when tables meet conversation\\. Tell the Agent \"check the product table and list everything with stock below 10\" — it queries the table, returns results, and even embeds a live preview in the conversation\\.\n\nLike Library, Multidimensional Tables are embedded from the original Basil system\\. Authorize once, and they stay in your left sidebar\\.\n\nTurning a pile of product photos into a structured spec sheet — that kind of real\\-world scenario comes later in the playbook\\.\n\n"
