        "title": "Sub-scenario B: Resume Screening & Matching — 100 Resumes, Ranked in 3 Minutes",
        "image": null,
        "markdown": "\n\n### Pain Point\n\n> \"200 resumes for one role\\. If I spend 5 minutes on each, that's 16 hours of screening\\. And I still miss great candidates\\.\"\n> \n> \n\n\n### Steps\n\n1. **Upload resumes**\nUpload a batch of resumes \\(PDF/Word\\) to the Workbench conversation\\.\n\n2. **AI auto\\-parses**\nThe AI reads each resume and extracts key info:\n\n    |    Field|    Description|\n    |---|---|\n    |    Name|    Full name|\n    |    Experience|    Total years of work|\n    |    Skills|    Industry tools, professional skills, software|\n    |    Languages|    Languages and proficiency|\n    |    Last employer|    Most recent company|\n    |    Current role|    Most recent job title|\n\n3. **Input job requirements, AI scores the match**\nTell the AI which role you're hiring for\\. It calculates a match score \\(0\\-100\\) for each candidate and ranks them\\.\n\n4. **Results written to the multidimensional table**\nThe match ranking table goes into the table\\. Hiring managers can view, filter, and sort\\. Original resume files \\(PDF/Word\\) can also be linked to the corresponding records\\.\n\n5. **Natural language follow\\-up queries**\nYou can filter candidates directly with natural language:\n\n```text\nList all candidates with 3+ years luxury experience, Italian B2 or above, currently in Milan. Sort by match score descending.\n```\n\n\n### Task Instruction\n\n```text\nParse the following resumes, extract key info (name, experience years, skills, languages, education, current role).\nMatch against the following job requirements:\n- Role: Senior Merchandiser\n- Requirements: 5+ years fashion industry, Italian native or C1+, English B2+, proficient in Excel and data analysis tools\n\nGenerate a match ranking table (0-100 points), write to the multidimensional table, including:\nName, Experience years, Current role, Last employer, Skills, Languages, Match score, Rank.\nLink original resume files to the corresponding records.\n```\n\n\n### Expected Results\n\n- All resumes auto\\-parsed, match scores clear at a glance\n\n- Multidimensional table supports filtering and sorting — hiring managers can view directly\n\n- You can query specific candidates using natural language\n\n\n### Advanced: Auto-update Interview Feedback\n\nAfter the interview, type your evaluation directly in Workbench:\n\n```text\nCandidate Marco Rossi interview feedback: Strong industry experience, deep understanding of merchandising, fluent English, Italian needs improvement. Result: proceeding to second round. Recommend scheduling a technical interview with the team lead.\n```\n\nThe AI auto\\-updates the feedback and result in the multidimensional table\\.\n\n\n### Advanced: Auto-reminder for Stale Candidates\n\nSet up a scheduled reminder: candidates not followed up within 7 days are auto\\-flagged and pushed to Teams:\n\n```text\nSet up reminder: In the multidimensional table, candidates with status \"Pending\" and no update for 7+ days should be auto-flagged in red and pushed to Teams for the recruiter.\n```\n\n> PS: Under GDPR and EU Anti\\-Discrimination Directive \\(2000/78/EC\\), personal data in resumes is sensitive\\. Ensure: 1\\) Only collect information directly relevant to the role; 2\\) Do not use age, gender, race, religion, or marital status as scoring criteria; 3\\) Retain candidate data only as long as needed for the hiring purpose \\(recommend deleting un\\-hired candidate data within 6 months\\)\\.\n> \n> \n\n"
