        "markdown": "\n\n### Pain Point\n\n> \"Supplier sends a 25\\-page T\\&C\\. I need to compare it line by line against our company standard terms\\. One contract takes 2 hours\\. Three contracts, and the day is gone\\.\"\n> \n> \n\n\n### Steps\n\n1. **Prepare standard terms**: Save your company's standard contract terms to Library \\(PDF or Word\\)\n\n2. **Upload supplier contract**: Upload the supplier's T\\&C to the conversation or Library\n\n3. **Instruct the Agent to compare**: Tell the Agent which documents are which, ask for a line\\-by\\-line comparison\n\n4. **Review the report**: The Agent outputs a difference report\\. Legal reviews and confirms\\.\n\n\n### Task Instruction\n\n```\nCompare the following two contracts and output a difference report:\nDocument 1 (Company Standard Terms): Library / Legal/Standard_Terms.pdf\nDocument 2 (Supplier T&C): Uploaded file Supplier_Terms.pdf\n\nComparison dimensions:\n1. Payment terms (terms, currency, penalties)\n2. IP ownership\n3. Confidentiality (scope, duration)\n4. Termination (conditions, notice period)\n5. Liability limitations\n6. Governing law and dispute resolution\n\nFor each dimension:\n- Mark differences (added / removed / modified)\n- Assign risk level (High / Medium / Low)\n- Provide 3 key negotiation suggestions\n\nOutput: Generate a Word difference report, clearly formatted and editable — legal team can annotate and modify directly. Also log this review in the \"Contract Review Records\" multidimensional table.\n```\n\n\n### Expected Results\n\n- Difference comparison table across 6 dimensions\n\n- Risk level assigned to each difference\n\n- 3 key negotiation suggestions\n\n- Difference report as a Word document, editable by legal, plus logged in the contract review table\n\n> 💡 The Agent does document comparison, not legal advice\\. Risk levels are based on clause differences\\. Final acceptance is up to the legal team\\. The Agent saves the line\\-by\\-line comparison time — it doesn't replace legal judgment\\.\n> \n> \n\n"
